{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 2, "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_seed": 2594979797081118980, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {"pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 637, "mtime": 1791865356.8228855, "sha256": "253c1372a397ab23c194cd32a5859ef638d7443af6ec141f043d3005362f6865"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-screen5-b2/omp-38/omp-38/transcripts/without/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/1/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 1, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-screen5-b2/omp-38/omp-38/cells/without/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/1/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Cause:** the float `2.675` is actually stored as `2.67499999999999982\u2026`, which is just under the halfway point. Python's built-in `round()` also rounds exact halves to the nearest even digit, not up. Both problems made it go down.\n\n**Fix** (`pricing/money.py`): `round_money` now does `Decimal(repr(x)).quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP)` and converts the result back to `float`. `repr(x)` gives the shortest decimal that maps back to the same float, which is `\"2.675\"`, so half-up rounding applies to the number the caller wrote. It still returns a `float`, so `add_vat` and other callers are unaffected.\n\n**Checked:**\n- 2.675 \u2192 2.68, 1.005 \u2192 1.01, 0.125 \u2192 0.13, 2.665 \u2192 2.67, \u22122.675 \u2192 \u22122.68, 2.674 \u2192 2.67.\n- `tests/test_split.py` passes. pytest isn't installed here, so I called `test_split()` directly.\n\n**Limit:** if a total is computed before rounding, e.g. `x * 1.2` inside `add_vat`, float error in the product can still push it to the wrong side of a half-cent. Only storing and calculating money as `Decimal` throughout would rule that out.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 7, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 139033, "requests_cache_write": 59263, "requests_cost_usd": 0.3580456, "requests_count": 7, "requests_input_uncached": 16, "requests_output": 1693, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-bugfix-regress:claude-opus-5-5:trial1", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 0, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T04:22:22.136714+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 24.439, "t_checker_s": 0.381, "t_env_setup_s": 0.002, "task": "trig-omp-bugfix-regress", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive", "adap